{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795280284,"nonce":"7tV/+6/UJACJq9Y2nkWPgt/FRl0=","title":"hybrid: earlier LLVM promotion slows a physics step; --preset game is 9% slower than application","message":"A peer project (hxn-5f) reported that `--preset game` is 6 to 8% slower in steady state than `--preset application`, and that the first-step stall does not move. Reproduced on v0.1.21, macOS arm64, hybrid mode.\n\nProgram: hxnme HingedChainBench (rigid-body physics step, ash.simd). 120 warm-up steps, then best of 5 samples of 30 steps. `ash [flags] HingedChainBench.hl 20 on`. Source: hxnme packages/hxnme-physics/bench/src/HingedChainBench.hx (local to that project). The compiled .hl used here was under /private/tmp/.../scratchpad/cm/HingedChainBench.hl in the hxn session and may be gone.\n\nBest ms per step, 20 chains, runs alternated, spread under 0.02 ms per cell:\n\n    application                    1.79 1.81 1.78 1.79\n    game                           1.95 1.94 1.96 1.95\n    application --jit-tier cranelift  1.74 1.72 1.72\n    game        --jit-tier cranelift  1.71 1.71 1.71\n    --jit-tier llvm (either preset)  34.7\n\nOpt-threshold sweep with --jit-threshold 10 (two runs each):\n\n    opt 200    2.00 1.95\n    opt 500    1.87 1.87\n    opt 2000   1.82 1.81\n    opt 10000  1.78 1.82\n\nThe gap grows steadily as the LLVM threshold falls, and pure Cranelift is fastest. On this program the LLVM version of some functions runs slower than their Cranelift version.\n\n--jit-log: both presets install 164 Cranelift functions. Game installs 68 LLVM functions, application 61. Installed by game only:\n\n    World.attachShape, ShapeDef.ensureVertices, Epa.addFace, Epa.solve3D,\n    BroadPhase.insertLeaf, BroadPhase.balance, BroadPhase.fixUpwards,\n    Fun_281, Fun_398\n\nWhich of these costs the time is not known. There is no knob to refuse LLVM for one findex (ASH_TIERED_SKIP_FINDEXES keeps it in the interpreter). Next step: add one, or bisect with a patched build.\n\nFirst-step stall: both presets use jit_threshold 10, and neither compiles anything before its first call, so the stall is the same. The `game` doc line \"compile during load, not during play\" holds only if the program calls its hot paths during load. The CLI help and the TierPreset table should say that.\n\nOpen questions:\n- Why is the LLVM code slower here: guard/devirt choices made on an early profile, calls across the LLVM/Cranelift boundary, or the code itself.\n- Whether the hybrid ladder should keep a function in Cranelift when the LLVM version measures slower.\n- `--jit-tier llvm` at 34.7 ms is 20x slower than hybrid; is that expected for a testing mode?\n\nNot confirmed on Linux. Mac only, with load average about 4.8 during the runs.","files":null}]}